                                "sense_id": "ae0579bb-84b7-34a0-aedf-cc493e1aca83",
                                "text": "Three-and-twenty years form a large portion of the short life of man,—one-third as nearly as can be expressed in unbroken numbers, of the entire term fixed by the psalmist, and full one-half, if we strike off the twilight of childhood and immature youth, and of senectitude weary of its toils."
